# Atexis Global Rules

## Security
- NEVER hardcode credentials, tokens, or secrets
- ALWAYS validate and sanitize user input
- Use parameterized queries for database access
- Apply principle of least privilege
- Log security events to audit trail

## Code Quality
- Write clear, readable code over clever code
- Follow existing project conventions and patterns
- Handle all error cases explicitly
- Use strong typing (TypeScript strict mode, Python type hints)
- No TODO/FIXME in committed code

## Architecture
- Respect separation of concerns
- Business logic belongs in services, not in route handlers
- Database access only through repository/model layer
- Configuration from environment, never hardcoded
- All state in database, not localStorage/sessionStorage

## Data Handling
- Respect data classification levels
- Never log PII or sensitive data
- Encrypt sensitive data at rest
- Use secure transport (HTTPS/TLS) for all communications
